nent/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span class=\"reference-title\">Cards: UI-Component Definition</span><span class=\"reference-source\">NN/g ↗</span></a><a class=\"reference-link\" href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_grid_layout/Auto-placement_in_grid_layout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span class=\"reference-title\">Auto-placement in CSS grid layout</span><span class=\"reference-source\">MDN ↗</span></a></div></section></div>","sourceUrl":"https://vibe-hub.org/en/card-grid-layout","markdown":"# Card Grid\n\nYou might say\nShow the content as cards in a grid, with more columns on wide screens and wrapping on narrow ones.\n\n**Arrange similar cards in a responsive grid**·A card grid helps people browse products, templates, articles, or projects with a shared visual structure. Define how columns change with width, keep card content comparable, and avoid forcing every card to the same height when content differs greatly.\nKnow first\n[Card](/vibe-hub/card?lang=en)[Grid](/vibe-hub/grid?lang=en)\n\n## You can say this to an AI Agent\n\n> “\n> Build the template list as a responsive card grid. Derive minimum card width from title, image, and actions, manage spacing with one gap, and reduce columns automatically. Test long titles, missing images, and mobile width.\n\n### When to use it\n\n- Product catalog\n\n**Wireless headphones**¥ 299\n\n**Mechanical keyboard**¥ 199\n- Template gallery\n- Project overview\n- Visual content browser\n\n### When NOT to use it\n\n- Use cards for dense field-by-field comparison\n- Keep too many columns on a phone\n- Give each card a completely different structure\n- Crop important content just to equalize every height\n\n✎★⬇⋯\n\nAnatomy\n\nCard\n\n1ContainerThe grid container, which defines the columns and spacing\n\n2CardCards with the same structure are easier to scan consistently\n\n3GapThe gaps between cards, declared once for the whole grid\n\nVariants\n\nAutoFill\n\nWhen the card has a reasonable minimum width and the number of columns needs to change with the container\n\nTwo Cols\n\nThe card contains a lot of content and requires a large preview\n\nThree Cols\n\nBackend list with stable content width\n\nTypical use cases\n\nProduct catalog\n\nMountain Camping App\n\nUI Design · 2025\n\n      \nProductivity Suite Website\n\nWeb Design · 2025\n\n      \nPet Community App\n\nProduct Design · 2024\n\nTemplate gallery\n\n🎧\n\n        \nNoise Canceling Headphones Pro\n\n**¥ 899**23,000 sold\n\n      \n⌨️\n\n        \nMechanical keyboard 87 keys\n\n**¥ 349**8,600 sold\n\n      \n💡\n\n        \nSmart eye protection desk lamp\n\n**¥ 199**Free shipping\n\nPortfolio\n\nSaaS landing page\n\nLanding · FreeUse\n\n      \nEvent registration page\n\nEvent · FreeUse\n\n      \nBlog theme\n\nBlog · ¥ 29Use\n\nProject list\n\nFilter\n\n      \n\n      \n\"Summer\" related materials 12,408 pieces · Sorted by popularity\n\nRecommended tool\n[Web fine-tuning tool · Selector Pro\n\n## Select page elements for precise AI edits\n\nClick a button, text, or card, note the change, then copy its exact location to AI.\nOpen Selector Pro website↗\n\nyour-site.com\n\n**Button · Get started**Use a smaller radius\n\nButton · Get started**Copied for AI**](https://selector-pro.org/)\n\nFurther reading\n\n[Cards: UI-Component DefinitionNN/g ↗](https://www.nngroup.com/articles/cards-component/)[Auto-placement in CSS grid layoutMDN ↗](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_grid_layout/Auto-placement_in_grid_layout)"}